  18) Type of Directories:
      1) bin(binaries) - Accessible for all the users, includes fundamental commands used for operate systems and perform day-to-day tasks like ls, cp, mv, rm, cat, etc
      2) sbin(system binaries) - Not accessible to regular users only system administrator(root user) can be accessed, includes powerful commands used for System recovery, Hardware configuration, Administration and System maintainance like fsck, reboot,  shutdown, etc. Regular users can be accessed with the elevated priveleges lide sudo.  
      3) boot - Contains files required to start the Linux operating system.
      4) dev - Contains special files representing devices and other kernel interfaces.
      5) etc - Contains system-wide configuration files.
      6) tmp - Stores temporary files created by applications and processes.
         
        
